  "rationale": "The answers are semantically correct. The national distinction is a preference distinction, not a strict mutual-exclusion claim: ayah tiri is attested in Malaysian official usage, while bapa tiri is the dictionary-listed Malaysian Malay equivalent. Available evidence does not establish that bapa tiri is an ordinary Indonesian preference or that ayah tiri displaces bapa tiri in Malaysian standard usage. No false-friend contrast is needed for these transparent, corresponding compounds.",
